chuckcar <chuckcar@nil.org> writes:
> Jukka Lahtinen <jtfjdehf@hotmail.com.invalid> wrote in

> > Use exit if you pressed ! when you got the prompt, but not after
> > ctrl-z. After ctrl-z, fg is the right command like others said.

> Yes, there *are* two methods alright, but it's actually fg nethack, not
> just fg by itself BTW. 

Just fg by itself returns to the latest process where you pressed ^Z.
For users not familiar with the ^Z suspend there is often only one such
process, but there MAY be more. 
The command jobs shows these processes, and the one marked with the +
character is the one where simple fg with no parameters will return.
You can return to the others with fg <number> where <number> can be seen
in the jobs output.
I just tried that "fg nethack" also works, hadn't known that kind of usage
before. 

